  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionCode": "book6-article-016-body",
      "heading": "Reading the Book VI structure",
      "anchor": "article-body",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Developmentalism linked economic growth, industrial capacity and state-building, while state-led industrialization concentrated capital, industry and infrastructure around long-term transformation goals. Similar instruments nevertheless produced different outcomes across societies."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The differences cannot be explained by policy labels alone. Implementation capacity, fiscal constraints, market scale, education, governance, international conditions and historical paths all change how the same instrument works in practice."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This article distinguishes historical fact, historical reconstruction and structural interpretation in the manuscript. Later outcomes are not treated as inevitable at the time, and motives or causal claims not present in the manuscript are not added."
        }
      ]
    }
